cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QForge in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "QForge: An Event-Driven Quantum Circuit Simulator in Java"
abstract: >-
  QForge is an exact quantum circuit simulator written in Java 17. It executes
  time-ordered quantum events against a state-vector backend (up to 30 qubits), a
  density-matrix backend (up to 12 qubits), an exact Clifford stabilizer tableau, or
  a truncated matrix-product-state backend. It applies Kraus noise plus device noise
  (T1/T2 relaxation, idle relaxation, crosstalk, and readout confusion), supports
  classical registers with conditional feed-forward and per-shot execution, imports
  and exports an OpenQASM 2.0/3.0 subset, measures arbitrary Hermitian observables
  with projective state collapse, and includes reference circuits for Grover search,
  the quantum Fourier transform, phase estimation, VQE, QAOA, arithmetic, amplitude
  amplification, Trotterized evolution, the Shor code, quantum walks, a quantum neural
  network, and a swap-test kernel classifier.
